{"blocks":[{"l":"header","b":[0.83,0.1093,0.9104,0.127],"t":"Listening"},{"l":"header","b":[0.1758,0.1502,0.5413,0.1691],"t":"SECTION 4 Questions 31–40"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1771,0.1817,0.3996,0.1994],"t":"Complete the notes below."},{"l":"header","b":[0.1771,0.21,0.5317,0.2277],"t":"Write ONE WORD ONLY for each answer."},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.2933,0.2448,0.7908,0.2672],"t":"Marine renewable energy (ocean energy)"},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.1913,0.2722,0.3075,0.2901],"t":"Introduction"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1908,0.2928,0.8554,0.3116],"t":"More energy required because of growth in population and 31 ....."},{"l":"text","b":[0.1921,0.3131,0.3279,0.3308],"t":"What's needed:"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1921,0.3343,0.4579,0.352],"t":"renewable energy sources"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1917,0.3543,0.5271,0.3726],"t":"methods that won't create pollution"},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.1921,0.3764,0.3146,0.3947],"t":"Wave energy"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1917,0.3968,0.8408,0.4156],"t":"Advantage: waves provide a 32 source of renewable energy"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1921,0.4171,0.7183,0.4362],"t":"Electricity can be generated using offshore or onshore systems"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1925,0.4383,0.5133,0.4563],"t":"Onshore systems may use a reservoir"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1929,0.4586,0.2833,0.476],"t":"Problems:"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1908,0.4795,0.6088,0.4969],"t":"• waves can move in any 33 ___"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1921,0.4996,0.8925,0.5178],"t":"movement of sand, etc. on the 34.....of the ocean may be affected"},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.1933,0.5219,0.3088,0.5396],"t":"Tidal energy"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1925,0.5426,0.5967,0.5596],"t":"Tides are more 35 ..... than waves"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1929,0.5626,0.4492,0.5803],"t":"Planned tidal lagoon in Wales:"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1913,0.5832,0.67,0.6006],"t":"• will be created in a 36 ..... at Swansea"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1908,0.6038,0.5725,0.6218],"t":"• breakwater (dam) containing 16 turbines"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1913,0.6242,0.7442,0.6427],"t":"- rising tide forces water through turbines, generating electricity"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1921,0.6451,0.8708,0.6772],"t":"• stored water is released through 37 ..... , driving the turbines in the reverse direction"},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.1929,0.681,0.3029,0.6981],"t":"Advantages:"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1913,0.7016,0.4579,0.7187],"t":"not dependent on weather"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1913,0.7216,0.6558,0.739],"t":"no 38 is required to make it work"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1913,0.7426,0.6396,0.7596],"t":"• likely to create a number of 39"},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.1929,0.7632,0.2742,0.7794],"t":"Problem:"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1925,0.7823,0.8938,0.8015],"t":"may harm fish and birds, e.g. by affecting 40 ..... and building up silt"},{"l":"paragraph_title","b":[0.1929,0.8047,0.4996,0.823],"t":"Ocean thermal energy conversion"},{"l":"text","b":[0.1921,0.8247,0.7775,0.8607],"t":"Uses a difference in temperature between the surface and lower levels\nWater brought to the surface in a pipe"},{"l":"number","b":[0.885,0.8666,0.9083,0.881],"t":"15"}]}